        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n  <title>Sacred Dance Guild 20th Anniversary Festival</title>\n  <script>\n    window.MathJax = {\n      tex: {\n        inlineMath: [['$', '$']],\n        displayMath: [['$$', '$$']]\n      }\n    };\n  </script>\n  <script async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n  <style>\n    * {\n      box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n\n    html,\n    body {\n      margin: 0;\n      min-height: 100%;\n      background: #e8e5dc;\n    }\n\n    body {\n      padding: 10px;\n      color: #191816;\n      font-family: \"Segoe Print\", \"Bradley Hand\", \"Comic Sans MS\", cursive;\n    }\n\n    .page {\n      width: min(1680px, 100%);\n      min-height: 2165px;\n      margin: 0 auto;\n      padding: 10px 112px 55px;\n      background:\n        radial-gradient(circle at 9% 8%, rgba(115, 99, 71, 0.05), transparent 18%),\n        radial-gradient(circle at 86% 47%, rgba(120, 102, 75, 0.045), transparent 24%),\n        linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(136, 119, 87, 0.035), transparent 5%, transparent 95%, rgba(136, 119, 87, 0.03)),\n        #f8f6ed;\n      box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(59, 51, 37, 0.12);\n      font-size: 30px;\n      font-weight: 600;\n      line-height: 1.54;\n      letter-spacing: 0;\n    }\n\n    .page-number {\n      margin: -4px 0 21px;\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 28px;\n      line-height: 1;\n    }\n\n    .festival-heading {\n      text-align: center;\n      font-size: 30px;\n      line-height: 1.68;\n    }\n\n    .festival-heading div {\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    .introduction {\n      margin-top: 42px;\n    }\n\n    .main-heading {\n      display: inline-block;\n      margin: 0 0 9px 8px;\n      border-bottom: 3px solid #201f1b;\n      font-size: 29px;\n      line-height: 1.18;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    .line {\n      min-height: 1.54em;\n      white-space: nowrap;\n    }\n\n    .intro-line {\n      margin-left: 4px;\n    }\n\n    .center-heading {\n      width: max-content;\n      margin: 21px auto 7px;\n      border-bottom: 3px solid #201f1b;\n      font-size: 29px;\n      line-height: 1.25;\n    }\n\n    .section {\n      margin-top: 0;\n    }\n\n    .section-label {\n      display: inline-block;\n      margin: 0 0 0 0;\n      border-bottom: 3px solid #201f1b;\n      font-size: 29px;\n      line-height: 1.25;\n    }\n\n    .entry-title {\n      display: inline-block;\n      border-bottom: 3px solid #201f1b;\n      line-height: 1.22;\n    }\n\n    .entry {\n      margin-top: 5px;\n    }\n\n    .entry .line {\n      margin-left: 84px;\n    }\n\n    .entry .line:first-child {\n      margin-left: 82px;\n    }\n\n    .biography {\n      margin-top: 12px;\n    }\n\n    .biography .line,\n    .consort-bio .line {\n      margin-left: 0;\n    }\n\n    .music {\n      margin-top: 13px;\n    }\n\n    .music-entry {\n      margin-top: 5px;\n    }\n\n    .music-entry .line {\n      margin-left: 80px;\n    }\n\n    .consort-bio {\n      margin-top: 11px;\n    }\n\n    u {\n      text-decoration-thickness: 2px;\n      text-underline-offset: 6px;\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 1200px) {\n      .page {\n        min-height: 0;\n        padding-right: 6.7%;\n        padding-left: 6.7%;\n        font-size: 1.75vw;\n      }\n\n      .page-number,\n      .festival-heading,\n      .main-heading,\n      .center-heading,\n      .section-label {\n        font-size: 1.7vw;\n      }\n    }\n\n    @media (max-width: 700px) {\n      body {\n        padding: 0;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n      }\n\n      .page {\n        width: 1000px;\n        padding-right: 67px;\n        padding-left: 67px;\n        font-size: 17.5px;\n      }\n\n      .page-number,\n      .festival-heading,\n      .main-heading,\n      .center-heading,\n      .section-label {\n        font-size: 17px;\n      }\n    }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main class=\"page\">\n    <div class=\"page-number\">- 34 -</div>\n\n    <header class=\"festival-heading\">\n      <div>Sacred Dance Guild 20th Anniversary Festival</div>\n      <div>Endicott College Beverly, Mass.</div>\n      <div>June 21-25, 1978</div>\n    </header>\n\n    <section class=\"introduction\">\n      <div class=\"main-heading\">The Variety and The Unity of Spiritual Gifts....1 Corinthians 12:4-7</div>\n\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">\"There is a variety of gifts but always the same Spirit; there are all sorts of service</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">to be done, but always to the same Lord; working in all sorts of different ways in different</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">people, it is the same God who is working in all of them......\"</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">Through the years the Sacred Dance Guild has offered leadership in a variety of dance</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">forms and religious denominations and with this 20th anniversary year we continue to</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">build on the foundation of both traditional and contemporary expression. With this</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">and in coming Festivals the culmination of the conference will be in the creating,</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">participation and experience of a particular denominational worship service and its</div>\n      <div class=\"line intro-line\">time in history.</div>\n    </section>\n\n    <div class=\"center-heading\">Artists In Leadership</div>\n\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Dance</div>\n\n      <div class=\"entry\">\n        <div class=\"line\"><span class=\"entry-title\">The Spirit Moves - A Workshop In Dance and Prayer</span> - Through the interaction of self,</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">improvisation and prayer the workshop will explore a variety of ways dance and prayer</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">can enhance liturgy and illuminate scripture varying with the feasts and seasons in</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">the church year allowing us to become more involved in the word of God as it touches us</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"biography\">\n        <div class=\"line\">Carla DeSola, a graduate of the Juilliard School of Music, has danced and given workshops</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">on dance and prayer from California to New York, for colleges, retreat centers, parishes</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">and religious conferences. She has produced for television, writes a monthly column on</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">dance for <u>Liturgy</u> and is the author of <u>Learning Through Dance</u> and <u>The Spirit Moves</u> ....</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">a handbook on dance and prayer. Presently she is teaching at the College of New Rochelle,</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">New York Theological Seminary and directing the Omega Liturgical Dance Company of New</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">York City.</div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <section class=\"section music\">\n      <div class=\"section-label\">Music</div>\n\n      <div class=\"music-entry\">\n        <div class=\"line\"><span class=\"entry-title\">Calliope Consort - Music for Worship and Dance</span> - Music from biblical times through</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">the 17th century will be played on medieval, renaissance, baroque and folk instru-</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">ments such as violas da gamba, recorders, krummhorns, pipe and tabor, percussion,</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">harp, rauschepfeiffe, psaltry and cornamuse.</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"consort-bio\">\n        <div class=\"line\">The Calliope Consort is directed by Nancy Nichols and assisted by Sybille Volz and members</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">of the Consort. The group has performed at the Museum of Fine Arts, Boston; The Fogg</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">Museum, Cambridge; the chapel at the Mass. General Hospital; before the Middlesex Health</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">Association; at lecture demonstrations and for many schools and libraries. In addition</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">to numerous church services, worship and wedding celebrations of a variety of denomina-</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">tions, they have participated in Shakespear's Twelfth Night as well as their own original</div>\n        <div class=\"line\">creation.</div>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>"
